// Part IV — Commands. Declared mode: reference.
page cmd_apply {
  sites = [:manual]
  title = "config-weave apply"

  chapter_header "config-weave apply" {
    kicker       = "Commands · reference"
    reading_time = "3 min read"
    updated      = "2026-10-30"
    version      = "config-weave 0.1.0"
  }

  p <<'PROSE'
`apply` converges one play. It validates the playbook, runs the play's gatherers, then walks the step DAG. Each step's `check` runs first. A step that is NotConfigured gets its `apply`, and then `check` runs again to confirm the result. A step whose second check does not report AlreadyConfigured is an Error. A wait step polls its probe instead, every `interval` until it reports ready or the step's `timeout` passes; see [Waiting for upstream systems](guide_waiting). See [The convergence contract](guide_convergence) for the full lifecycle and [Check, then apply](howto_check_apply) for the recommended workflow.
PROSE

  h2 "Synopsis"

  code console {
    source = <<'SRC'
config-weave apply [OPTIONS] <PLAYBOOK_DIR> <PLAY>
SRC
  }

  h2 "Arguments"

  table {
    rows:
      | "Argument" | "Meaning" |
      | "`PLAYBOOK_DIR`" | "The playbook directory, containing `playbook.wcl`." |
      | "`PLAY`" | "The name of the play to apply. `config-weave list` shows the names." |
  }

  h2 "Options"

  p "All [global options](cmd_root) apply. The variable, password, worker pool, error and output options all take effect here."

  table {
    rows:
      | "Option" | "Value" | "Meaning" |
      | "`--events-ndjson`" | "" | "Stream one JSON event per line to stderr: run and gather lifecycle plus per-step phase progress. Replaces the live progress line. Stdout still carries the final report, so combine with `--json` for a fully machine-readable run." |
      | "`--continue-on-error`" | "" | "Keep dispatching steps after an Error instead of halting once in-flight steps finish. Without it, a halt cancels wait steps at their next pause between probe attempts." |
      | "`--jobs`" | "`N`" | "Worker pool size. Wait steps run outside the pool and do not count against it. See [Scheduling and concurrency](guide_scheduling)." |
  }

  h2 "Events"

  p "With `--events-ndjson`, `check` and `apply` write one JSON object per line to stderr. Every event carries `event` and a `ts` timestamp in milliseconds."

  table {
    rows:
      | "Event" | "Fields" | "When" |
      | "`run_started`" | "`play`, `mode`, `steps` (each with `name`, `resource`, `container_path`)" | "Once, before the gatherer phase." |
      | "`gather_started`" | "`unique`, the number of distinct gatherer invocations" | "Before the gatherers run." |
      | "`gather_finished`" | "" | "After the gatherers run." |
      | "`step_started`" | "`idx`, `name`" | "A step is dispatched." |
      | "`step_phase`" | "`idx`, `name`, `phase`" | "A step enters a phase: `checking`, `applying`, `re-checking`, or `waiting` for a wait step." |
      | "`step_waiting`" | "`idx`, `name`, `attempt`, `elapsed_secs`, `timeout_secs`, `error`" | "A wait step's probe attempt was unsuccessful and the step will try again. `error` is `null` when the probe reported not ready, and the probe's message when it failed." |
      | "`step_finished`" | "`idx`, `name`, `container_path`, `resource`, `status`, `message`, `duration_secs`" | "A step reached its final status. For a wait step, `resource` is the probe reference." |
      | "`step_resolved`" | "`idx`, `name`, `status`" | "A step resolved without running, such as `skipped` or `not_run`." |
  }

  code json {
    source = <<'SRC'
{"event":"step_waiting","idx":0,"name":"api_up","attempt":3,"elapsed_secs":60.0,"timeout_secs":10800.0,"error":null,"ts":1793312977241}
SRC
  }

  h2 "Examples"

  p "Converge the `baseline` play."

  code console {
    source = <<'SRC'
config-weave apply ./my-playbook baseline
SRC
  }

  p "Apply with a variable override and a machine-readable report, then inspect the exit code."

  code console {
    source = <<'SRC'
config-weave apply ./my-playbook baseline --var hostname=web01 --json > report.json
echo $?
SRC
  }

  p "Apply a playbook that holds encrypted values, reading the password from a file, and log everything to NDJSON."

  code console {
    source = <<'SRC'
config-weave apply ./my-playbook baseline \
  --password-file /run/secrets/weave \
  --log-file /var/log/config-weave.ndjson --log-level debug
SRC
  }

  h2 "Exit status"

  p <<'PROSE'
0 when every step is Configured, Already Configured or Skipped. 1 when any step ended in Error, including a step whose apply succeeded but whose re-check disagreed, and a wait step that timed out. 2 when validation failed, a variable or password could not be resolved, or the play does not exist. 3 when a step returned RebootRequired and no step errored: the play halted, and running `apply` again after the reboot resumes it.
PROSE
}
